#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-ai-share: Share this device's AI (docs/AI-SHARE.md). Each Hearth device runs its own AI jobs whole (the Nvidia
PC big chat and pictures, the ROG Ally voices, a laptop speech-to-text) and, when you turn it on, says what it has at
one small read-only address over Tailscale. Your Home server lists every device's AI there too, and the Hearth AI
Command Center reads it to pick the best device for each job.

  hearth-ai-share status                 JSON for Settings: your choices, what's found here, the address, the service
  hearth-ai-share info                   this device's answer (the same JSON as GET /v1/hearth/ai)
  hearth-ai-share devices                every device's AI (the same JSON as GET /v1/hearth/ai/devices)
  hearth-ai-share set KEY on|off         on (Share this device's AI), hub (Let the Command Center find my devices here),
                                         lan (also on my home network), pluggedOnly, notWhilePlaying, codeOn,
                                         chat, voice, image, stt (which services to share)
  hearth-ai-share code-set               a share code on stdin (HEARTH_INPUT): 8-64 characters; only its hash is kept
  hearth-ai-share code-clear             no share code any more (codeOn goes off)
  hearth-ai-share move NAME up|down      the order the Command Center tries your devices in
  hearth-ai-share order-reset            back to the default order (a device with an Nvidia card first)
  hearth-ai-share apply                  the service and its firewall rule as your choices say (Settings runs it)
  hearth-ai-share serve                  the server (hearth-ai-share.service, your own user service)

The server answers on port 8189: GET /v1/hearth/ai (this device) and GET /v1/hearth/ai/devices (every device, when
"Let the Command Center find my devices here" is on). Read only, no secrets, nothing else. It listens on this device
(127.0.0.1) and on its Tailscale address only once Hearth's firewall rule is loaded (hearth-ai-share-helper, the
nftables table inet hearth_ai_share: lo and tailscale0 let in, everything else dropped on 8189); with "also on my home
network" on every address. Requests from anywhere but this device and Tailscale are refused unless you chose that.

Settings: ~/.config/nimbus/ai-share.json through hearth_settings_io (only the key you changed; atomic, .bak, merged
under the lock; defaults filled in when read, never saved). The share code's hash is state
(~/.local/state/nimbus/ai-share.json, 0600); devices seen before are a cache (~/.cache/nimbus/ai-share-devices.json).
Nothing here ever changes a setting by itself. Output: one JSON line; failures print "error: ..." and exit 1.
"""
